Kingdom's sovereign is the ghost of Qin Shihuangdi, and he got in the afterlife what he didn't quite manage to get in life - lasting dominion and rule over ghosts. Maybe. There's an implication that a Neverborn might be wearing his likeness like an ectoplasm suit, given that Oda Nobunaga's ghost faced him in a duel during WW2 and cut Qin in half... only for a giant pale jade dragon thought vanquished by the alleged Yu Huang early in his rule of the dead emerged and started wrecking shit, Nobunaga's ghost being the first one to go. The official line is that he can control the Neverborn Lung Wang, and you know, those imperial censors would never lie about something so important, wink wink nudge nudge say no more.<br /> <br /> So ghosts in the region are going to be involved in a mostly quiet war over antiquities thought unimportant, which are actually fetters, along with potential threats to the families of either side that still reside among the quick, Rebels against Yu Huang are going to typically try to extort supplies from an imperial official, while the other side is primarily going to perpetrate reprisal attacks to crush resistance to the ghostly emperor (and probably get a supply of ghostly jade bricks in the process), and occasionally attempt to suss out rebel plans and hideouts to send in the Immortal Guard to wipe the floor with them.<br /> <br /> As for making a kind of wraith fetish, that's not usually something within the bounds of what fetish makers can do (elemental and inauspicious instruments use living spirits), but if it is possible, it's way less binding and permanent than soulforging, since anything that can break the fetish will release the spirit. The existence of the Inhabit Arcanos, however, tends to suggest that it's the usual way for how wraiths stow away in objects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 01-18-2017, 09:06 PM"},"at